ut the most extreme  mutations are brought on by an  irradiated strain of illness called  necrosis which subjects its host to even  more rapid evolutionary changes while  the disease often results in  advantageous mutations it simultaneously  reduces the host's lifespan making it  more of a curse than a blessing the  necrosis infection has become a  widespread issue in various regions  contaminating a significant percentage  of the post-war biosphere  the region we'll be exploring in this  video was once the United Kingdom yet  the green Landscapes of old have been  replaced by a grim Wasteland of Silent  Decay The People's Spirit remains  hopeful however resulting in the  Region's nickname The Unbroken Kingdom  for among the small pockets of survivors  hope is the last defense against the  dangers of the new world  in the new reality of The Unbroken  Kingdom Farms of old no longer exist  with most domesticated animals unable to  survive in the merciless new paradigm  new animals have assumed the role of  livestock in the settlements that have  risen From the Ashes the mighty bulwark  are a widespread species of farm animal  that are quite docile despite what their  horns and tusks might suggest these  mammals are related to pre-war cows  namely the Holstein Friesian in the  Highland cattle breeds with adults known  to weigh well over a ton bulb worker  classified as megafauna and have the  tenacity needed to endure the  unforgiving post-war reality taking a  closer look at the bulwarks hide we can  see that their thick leathery skin acts  as a kind of natural body armor while  they retain The Familiar pattern of  their bovine ancestors the bulwark's  protective hide is closer to that of an  old world rhino post-warf Farmers rear  bulwarks on the fertile fields around a  region called new Yorkshire making the  area one of the more prosperous in The  Unbroken Kingdom  yet bulwarks aren't the only new farm  animal found within the meager  settlements of the Kingdom The Uncanny  bone hens are a common sight in this new  world their cretaceous-esque features  make them well adapted to the harsh  environment with the bonehead spikes  helping them stay cool during heat waves  boneheads serve as a replacement for the  chickens of the old world and have  changed much from their tame  predecessors their beak is deceptively  strong designed to crush eggshells and  other discarded scraps for an easy  source of protein comparing a bone hens  feathers to the plumage of an old world  chicken it becomes clear that the bone  hands feathers are significantly more  fused and matted their makeup is almost  more akin to the hardened scales of a  reptile than the soft plumage of a bird  due to a shortage of food the surviving  government has released posters urging  civilians to rear bone hens as a source  of sustenance while eating a mutated  species like a bone hen is a viable  means of staying alive in Desperate  Times the long-term effects of consuming  such meals remain to be seen  just beyond the fences far more  dangerous life forms prowl the ruined  Countryside in some regions of The  Unbroken Kingdom hazard signs warn  travelers to stay clear of nearby Zager  nests mid-sized Predators the zaggers  are a well-known threat found all across  the former British Isles with  bone-crushing jaws in a poisonous Barb  on the end of their tail Sanders are the  bane of unwary Travelers who stray too  far from the path yet surprisingly these  deadly animals are the descendants of  the harmless pre-war Badger which grew  in size and ferocity to adapt to an  unforgiving World modern zaggers are  almost entirely hairless giving them a  wrinkled appearance closer analysis of  their glaborous skin indicates their  baldness is likely due to an amino acid  substitution in a hair growth Associated  protein an analogous pre-war mutation  had occurred in naked mole rats  resulting in their characteristic lack  of visible fur while unsettling in  appearance the 