 Adept at  Scavenging for food unlike most pre-war  rodents however Dillo pigs have evolved  thick armor plating on their backs to  Shield against the predators of the  waste these hardened scales resemble the  protective leathery shell of Old World  armadillo species from which the Dillo  pigs get their nickname dillu pigs are  also known to create concealed nests  within pre-war ruins which they Retreat  into when threats arise and with  thousands of miles of abandoned piping  still present underground Dillo pigs  have plenty of room to make their  Burrows  thankfully the Dillo pig is one of the  few animals left in the world that could  be considered pet-like due to their  harmless nature and relatively cute  appearance  those who make their homes in the ruins  of urban areas must deal with other  types of animals gold wings are a  species of city-dwelling bat associated  with the growing region of New Yorkshire  despite their somewhat startling  appearance gold wings aren't aggressive  towards humans the descendants of  pre-war bats they feed primarily on  insects and other small organisms their  name comes from the golden hue of their  vibrant Wings which might serve as  camouflage against the ambient light of  cities most gold wings hunt by hanging  off lampposts and staying completely  still waiting for pests to run into the  open only to end up as an easy meal  because gold wings feed on  disease-carrying pests they've been  marked as an asset by the government of  The Unbroken Kingdom and are considered  a protected species as a result the  hunting of any gold wings within the  limits of new Yorkshire will earn  offenders a hefty fine  just beyond the outer limits of urban  areas scavengers lurk on the edges of  civilization the rot fowl or massive  birds that stand taller than a person  and feed on any carcasses that come  their way no matter how rotten or how  fresh often seen feasting upon remains  from local skirmishes they have earned  the nickname birds of war the descendant  of a pre-war bird of prey the rot fowl  had become larger and more terrestrial  than their ancestors having converged  Upon A towering body plan similar to The  Fearsome cassowaries of the old world to  match their unpleasant diet their beaks  had become sharp and hook-like get  rotfowl actually play a key role in  decomposition within their environment  like vultures the function they serve  within the food web might be on  glamorous yet it is fundamental to  various ecosystems for rotfowl don't  just affect the health of The Unbroken  Kingdom studies of their migratory  patterns indicate that rotfowl travel  across the North Sea once a year roaming  in large groups to other lands during  the height of their mating season  genetic mutations are responsible for  most of the fauna found Across The  Unbroken Kingdom yet the greatest  horrors of the wastes are in fact the  result of pre-war experiments conducted  by a company called biophageage a  clandestine organization with a long  history of ethical and moral violations  their Story begins long before the war  started originally formed as a  pharmaceutical Corporation the company  found its sales began to falter over the  decades everything changed however when  biophageage was taken over by one Dr  ellingham a successful businessman with  no background in biology and no  intention of engaging in ethical science  under his leadership biophage pivoted to  become a company on The Cutting Edge of  pre-war bioengineering the exact nature  of the early pre-war company experiments  is largely unknown and perhaps that is  for the best for what we do have on  record is bone chilling  not long before the outbreak of the war  biophage under the oversight of Dr  ellingham began experimenting with  medical Rejuvenation unit 151 would  become one of these many attempts  nicknamed ankle biters some of these  experiments could be considered  technically successful as the ankle  biters were able to regrow lost limbs as  intended yet the results were life forms  that could no longer be considered human  still biophage might have increased the  scale of these experiments were it not  for the violent claps of pre-war Society  yet not all experiments were destroyed  during the war some creations of  biophage escaped into the barren waste  and have been able to carve out a niche  in the brutal new natural hierarchy  today perhaps no life form in The  Unbroken kingdom is more dangerous than  the seldom scene biophageage experiment  that stalks the open Plains vespores are  ruthless bioweapons capable of Horrors  far beyond any naturally evolved form of  life while the original intention behind  their creation remains unknown the  results of the experiment are visible to  all  vespore's hunt with a stinger-like  appendage capable of spearing  fast-moving prey once an animal has been  speared the vespore then prepares to  digest The Unlucky creature the internal  anatomy of a vespore allows them to  digest prey directly through their  abdomen making them extremely efficient  as they are able to Feast while on the  move the terrifying behavior of the  vespor coupled with its elusive Nature  has caused it to take on an almost  mythical status in the minds of the  survivors for not many CIA vespor and  live to tell the tale  aside from terrifying monsters there is  a quiet sadness that the world of Baron  evokes it's hard not to read through the  project and feel a certain Melancholy  for all that has been lost bustling  towns healthy forests clean rivers much  of the world as it existed before the  apocalypse has changed utterly and might  never return to normal yet the people of  this alternate timeline have adapted to  the changes much like the strange fauna  that now roamed the Wilderness The  Unbroken Kingdom might be an unfamiliar  landscape but so long as it's possible  to continue to endure it will never be a  broken one there's much more to the  baron project than I w